  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are a warrior and you have to fight NNN enemy warriors (numbered 111 through NNN) one by one, in any order you choose. You have to win as many of these fights as possible.\n\nEach warrior has some amount of power, which changes when the warrior fights. For each iii, the iii-th enemy warrior has power PiP_iPi​. When you have power xxx and you fight an enemy warrior with power yyy, the following happens:\n\n\nif x&gt;yx \\gt yx&gt;y, you kill the enemy warrior and your power changes to 2(x−y)2(x-y)2(x−y)\notherwise (if x≤yx \\le yx≤y), the enemy warrior kills you\nYou should answer QQQ queries. In each query, you are given your initial power XXX and you should find the maximum number of warriors you can kill if you are starting with power XXX.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N,Q≤1051 \\le N, Q \\le 10^51≤N,Q≤105",
      "1≤Pi≤1091 \\le P_i \\le 10^91≤Pi​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "1≤X≤1091 \\le X \\le 10^91≤X≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​.\nQQQ lines follow. Each of these lines contains a single integer XXX describing a query.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query, print a single line containing one integer — the maximum number of warriors you can kill.",
    "notes": [],
